Article 4: A property reporting order shall specify the following matters:
(1) the time limit for submitting the property report;
(2) the scope and period of property to be reported;
(3) the conditions and time limit for supplementary property reporting;
(4) the legal liability to be borne for violating the obligation to report property;
(5) other matters the People's Court deems necessary to specify.
The property reporting order shall be accompanied by a property investigation form, and the party subject to enforcement must fill it out item by item in accordance with the requirements.

Article 5: The party subject to enforcement shall, within the time limit specified in the property reporting order, report in writing to the People's Court the following property:
(1) income, bank deposits, cash, wealth management products, and negotiable securities;
(2) real property such as land-use rights and houses;
(3) movable property such as means of transport, machinery and equipment, products, and raw materials;
(4) property rights such as claims, equities, investment interests, fund shares, trust beneficial rights, and intellectual property;
(5) other property that shall be reported.
Where the property of the party subject to enforcement is leased, has established security interests or other encumbrances, or is subject to co-ownership or ownership disputes, such circumstances shall also be reported; where the movable property of the party subject to enforcement is possessed by a third party, or the real property, specific movable property, or other property rights of the party subject to enforcement are registered in the name of a third party, such circumstances shall also be reported.
Where the party subject to enforcement truly has difficulty in submitting a written report within the time limit specified in the property reporting order, it may apply in writing to the People's Court for an extension; if the application has justifiable reasons, the People's Court may extend the time limit appropriately.

Article 6: Where, during the period from one year before the date on which the party subject to enforcement receives the enforcement notice to the date of submitting the written property report, the party's property undergoes any of the following changes, it shall report such changes together:
(1) transferring or leasing property;
(2) establishing security interests or other encumbrances on property;
(3) waiving claims or extending the time limit for payment of claims;
(4) expending large amounts of funds;
(5) other property changes affecting the realization of the claims determined in the effective legal instrument.

Article 11: The property reporting procedure shall be terminated under any of the following circumstances:
(1) the party subject to enforcement has fully performed the obligations determined in the effective legal instrument;
(2) the People's Court rules to terminate the enforcement;
(3) the People's Court rules not to enforce;
(4) other circumstances under which the People's Court considers that the property reporting procedure shall be terminated.
After a property reporting order is issued, if the People's Court rules to terminate the current enforcement procedure, the party subject to enforcement shall still perform the supplementary reporting obligation in accordance with Article 7 of these Provisions.

Article 21: Where the party subject to enforcement fails to perform the obligations determined in an effective legal instrument, the applicant for enforcement may apply in writing to the People's Court to issue a reward announcement to search for executable property. The application shall specify the following matters:
(1) the amount of the reward or the method of calculation;
(2) the acceptance that relevant personnel will voluntarily pay the reward when they provide property leads not yet known to the People's Court and the applicant's claim is thereby realized in whole or in part;
(3) the method of publishing the reward announcement;
(4) other matters that need to be specified.
The People's Court shall decide whether to permit it within ten days from the date of receipt of the written application.
